IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-pilot-elections`

-- Tests of er5-pilot-elections (regs 77.96, 77.98 and 77.991). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Regulations
-- (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1528-1539, 1549-1559 and 1569-1575), beside each assertion, before the run. Dates were checked against Python's datetime where a weekday or a sum of days matters.

§ `Purposes (src:1528, 1549, 1569)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.96(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 18 beyond its own` EQUALS "test which method, the one described in subsection 77.94(3) or the one described in subsection 77.95(3), is more effective in encouraging claimants to work more while receiving benefits"
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 19 beyond its own` EQUALS "test which method, the one described in subsection 77.94(3) or the one described in subsection 77.97(3), is more effective in encouraging claimants to work more while receiving benefits"
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 20 beyond its own` EQUALS "test which method, the one described in subsection 77.94(3) or the one described in subsection 77.99(3), is more effective in encouraging claimants to work more while receiving benefits"

§ `The method that results (src:1529, 1534, 1550, 1557, 1570)`

-- The argument order is: the claimant may elect; elects to have 77.94(3) apply; the election is considered made by the deadline; a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(2), (5), reg 77.98(2), (7) and reg 77.991(2) the method of treating the earnings of the benefit period` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er5 the allowable earnings method of subsection 77.94(3)`
-- Bound by a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period: the 50% deduction.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(2), (5), reg 77.98(2), (7) and reg 77.991(2) the method of treating the earnings of the benefit period` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `er5 the 50 percent deduction method of the pilot project for the period`
-- May not elect; did not elect; elected too late.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(2), (5), reg 77.98(2), (7) and reg 77.991(2) the method of treating the earnings of the benefit period` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er5 the 50 percent deduction method of the pilot project for the period`
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(2), (5), reg 77.98(2), (7) and reg 77.991(2) the method of treating the earnings of the benefit period` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er5 the 50 percent deduction method of the pilot project for the period`
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(2), (5), reg 77.98(2), (7) and reg 77.991(2) the method of treating the earnings of the benefit period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er5 the 50 percent deduction method of the pilot project for the period`

§ `The portion of a benefit period within a period (src:1529)`

-- The argument order is: the benefit period; the period. The period of reg 77.96 runs August 5, 2012 to August 1, 2015.
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.96 the portion of the benefit period that falls within the period` (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2012 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5), (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5), (YearMonthDay 2012 12 31))
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.96 the portion of the benefit period that falls within the period` (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1), (YearMonthDay 2016 2 1)) (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5), (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1), (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1))
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.96 the portion of the benefit period that falls within the period` (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2013 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2013 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5), (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2013 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2013 12 31))
-- Ends the day before the period begins: nothing in it. Ends on the first day: one day in it.
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.96 the portion of the benefit period that falls within the period` (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2012 8 4)) (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5), (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.96 the portion of the benefit period that falls within the period` (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5)) (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5), (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5), (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5))
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.96 the portion of the benefit period that falls within the period` (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2015 8 2), (YearMonthDay 2016 1 1)) (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5), (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.96 the later of two days` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 1 2
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.96 the earlier of two days` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 1 1

§ `The late election (src:1533, 1556, 1574)`

-- The argument order is: the day the claimant informs the Commission, if they do; the deadline; good cause is shown for the delay.
-- On the deadline itself: in time.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(4), reg 77.98(6) and reg 77.991(6) the election is considered to have been made by the deadline` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5)) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A day late with no good cause: not made by the deadline. A day late with good cause shown: considered made.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(4), reg 77.98(6) and reg 77.991(6) the election is considered to have been made by the deadline` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 6)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5)) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(4), reg 77.98(6) and reg 77.991(6) the election is considered to have been made by the deadline` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 6)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5)) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Never informed: not made.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(4), reg 77.98(6) and reg 77.991(6) the election is considered to have been made by the deadline` NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5)) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Informed, but no deadline is determined: the text gives none to be late for.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(4), reg 77.98(6) and reg 77.991(6) the election is considered to have been made by the deadline` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 6)) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 77.96 - Pilot Project No. 18 (src:1528-1539)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.96(2) the claimant may elect` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.96(2) the claimant may elect` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(2) the election is irrevocable` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.96(2) the election is irrevocable` FALSE)
-- (3). The argument order is: a notification issued from August 5, 2012 to January 5, 2013; a notification issued after January 5, 2013; the day the last notification is issued.
-- (a) alone: February 5, 2013 or 30 days after the last notification (October 1, 2012 plus 30 is October 31, 2012), whichever is later: February 5, 2013.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 10 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5)
-- (a) alone, the last notification on January 5, 2013: 30 days later is February 4, 2013, so February 5, 2013 is later.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2013 1 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5)
-- (b): a notification after January 5, 2013, the last on January 6, 2013: 30 days later is February 5, 2013, earlier than August 1, 2015.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2013 1 6) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5)
-- (b): the last notification on March 1, 2013: March 31, 2013.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2013 3 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 3 31)
-- (b): February 3, 2013 plus 30 days is March 5, 2013 (February 2013 has 28 days).
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2013 2 3) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 3 5)
-- (b): the last notification on July 20, 2015: 30 days later is August 19, 2015, but the earlier of the two days is August 1, 2015.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 7 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)
-- Notifications under both (a) and (b): (b) is applied (the reading taken): August 1, 2015, not August 19, 2015.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 7 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)
-- No notification in either period: no deadline given.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5) to (7). The argument order is: no election for an earlier benefit period by its deadline; the claimant had earnings in its weeks; the notification exception of (7).
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(5), (6) and (7) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- (6): no earnings in the weeks of the earlier benefit period.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.96(5), (6) and (7) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (7): notified from August 5 to October 6, 2012, and not after: not bound.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.96(5), (6) and (7) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- An election was made in time: nothing to be bound by.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.96(5), (6) and (7) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (8): no appeal under section 114 through March 31, 2013; no reconsideration under section 112 from April 1, 2013.
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(8)(a) the decision is not subject to appeal under section 114 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2012 9 1)
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(8)(a) the decision is not subject to appeal under section 114 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2013 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.96(8)(a) the decision is not subject to appeal under section 114 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2013 4 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.96(8)(b) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2013 3 31))
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(8)(b) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2013 4 1)
#ASSERT `reg 77.96(8)(b) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2014 1 1)

§ `Reg 77.98 - Pilot Project No. 19 (src:1549-1559)`

-- (2). The argument order is: had earnings subject to 77.94(3) from August 7, 2011 to August 4, 2012; made every election they were entitled to make under 77.96 (with the carve-out).
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(2) the claimant may elect` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.98(2) the claimant may elect` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.98(2) the claimant may elect` FALSE TRUE)
-- (3). The argument order is: an election was made under 77.96; the day the last notification is issued.
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(3) the election under section 77.96 is deemed to apply to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period within the period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 8 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.98(3) the election under section 77.96 is deemed to apply to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period within the period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.98(3) the election under section 77.96 is deemed to apply to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period within the period` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2015 9 1))
-- (4). The argument order is: an election was made under 77.98(2); the day the benefit period began.
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(4) the election also applies to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period before August 2, 2015` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.98(4) the election also applies to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period before August 2, 2015` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 8 2))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.98(4) the election also applies to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period before August 2, 2015` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2015 1 1))
-- (5): 30 days after the last notification, or August 6, 2016 (a Saturday), whichever is earlier. May 1, 2016 plus 30 is May 31, 2016.
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(5) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of their election` (YearMonthDay 2016 5 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2016 5 31
-- July 7, 2016 plus 30 is August 6, 2016 exactly; July 6 plus 30 is August 5; July 20 plus 30 is August 19, past the closing day.
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(5) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of their election` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 7) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2016 8 6
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(5) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of their election` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 6) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2016 8 5
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(5) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of their election` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2016 8 6
-- (7) and (8). The argument order is: no election for an earlier benefit period by its deadline; the claimant had earnings in its weeks.
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(7) and (8) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.98(7) and (8) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.98(7) and (8) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` FALSE TRUE)
-- (9)
#ASSERT `reg 77.98(9) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.98(9) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` FALSE)

§ `Reg 77.991 - Pilot Project No. 20 (src:1569-1575)`

-- (3). The argument order is: an election was made under 77.98; the day the last notification is issued.
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(3) the election under section 77.98 is deemed to apply to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period within the period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.991(3) the election under section 77.98 is deemed to apply to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period within the period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 6))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.991(3) the election under section 77.98 is deemed to apply to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period within the period` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2016 9 1))
-- (4). The argument order is: eligible to elect under 77.98; the day the benefit period began; the day it ended, if it has; the day the last notification is issued.
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(4) the claimant may make an election under subsection 77.991(2) in respect of the benefit period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 6) NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7)
-- "Has not ended on or before that day" (August 7, 2016): ended that day is out; ended the next day is in.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.991(4) the claimant may make an election under subsection 77.991(2) in respect of the benefit period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 6) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7)) (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7))
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(4) the claimant may make an election under subsection 77.991(2) in respect of the benefit period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 6) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 8 8)) (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7)
-- Began on August 7, 2016 itself: not "before August 7, 2016".
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.991(4) the claimant may make an election under subsection 77.991(2) in respect of the benefit period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7) NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7))
-- The last notification is issued before August 7, 2016.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.991(4) the claimant may make an election under subsection 77.991(2) in respect of the benefit period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 6) NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2016 8 6))
-- Not eligible to elect under 77.98.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.991(4) the claimant may make an election under subsection 77.991(2) in respect of the benefit period` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 6) NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7))
-- (5): 30 days after the last notification, or August 11, 2018, whichever is earlier. January 1, 2017 plus 30 is January 31, 2017.
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(5) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of their election` (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2017 1 31
-- July 12, 2018 plus 30 is August 11, 2018 exactly; July 13 plus 30 is August 12, past the closing day.
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(5) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of their election` (YearMonthDay 2018 7 12) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2018 8 11
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(5) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of their election` (YearMonthDay 2018 7 13) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2018 8 11
-- (7)
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(7) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.991(7) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` FALSE)
-- (2): the portion of a benefit period from January 1, 2016 to June 30, 2017 that falls within August 7, 2016 to August 11, 2018.
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(2) the portion of the benefit period to which the claimant may apply an election` (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2016 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2017 6 30)) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7), (YearMonthDay 2017 6 30))
#ASSERT `reg 77.991(2) the portion of the benefit period to which the claimant may apply an election` (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2018 8 12), (YearMonthDay 2019 1 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
